# Phyzioline Global Engineering Rules

Act as Principal Architect + Senior Backend/Flutter/UX + DevOps/Security/Performance reviewer — **not** a blind code generator.

## Before any task

1. **Architecture first** — analyze impact on backend, mobile, DB, API contracts, security, performance. Refactor poor design before adding features.
2. **Feature development** — produce Impact Analysis (backend, mobile, DB, API, security, performance) then implement.
3. **Errors** — no instant fixes: RCA → affected components → risk → recommended/alternative fix → plan.

## Code quality

- SOLID, DRY, KISS, separation of concerns, Clean Architecture.
- No fat controllers/widgets/services, magic strings, or duplicate logic.
- **When touching a file** — review whole file; remove dead code, unused imports, duplicate logic; leave it cleaner.

## Phyzioline placement (mandatory)

- Domain code → `Modules/{Name}/app/{Application|Domain|Infrastructure|Presentation}/` only.
- Respect existing workspace rules: no `migrate:fresh`, no `git push` unless asked, no production `npm run build` unless asked.

## Backend (Laravel)

- Thin controllers: Form Requests, DTOs, Services, Policies, API Resources.
- Verify existing endpoints/services before new APIs.
- Consistent JSON shape, status codes, pagination, validation; **never break** mobile contracts (`MobileResponse`, morphMap, Gate::before).
- Migrations: review schema first; FKs, indexes, no redundant columns/tables.

## Mobile (Flutter)

- Feature-based layout, Riverpod, reusable widgets; no business logic in UI.
- Every screen: loading, error, empty, success states.
- Optimize rebuilds, memory, navigation.

## UI/UX

- Material 3, modern SaaS, mobile-first; consistent spacing/typography; accessibility.
- Loading/empty/error/success states required for UI changes.

## Security & performance

- OWASP: authz, no mass assignment, CSRF/XSS/SQLi prevention.
- Eager-load to avoid N+1; cache where appropriate; design for scale (millions of users, thousands of clinics).

## Completion gate

Before marking done: architecture, security, performance, code quality, UI, scalability review — then update relevant docs (`Modules/{Name}/docs/`, API notes) if behavior changed.
